      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXXXVI.—Anushṭub.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXXXVII.— विप्लुताः = afflicted, ruined comp. प्रजाविप्लवः in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Mahâvîracharita (Trith.) p. 48 or आचारस्य विप्लवम् Ditto.—Gîti.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXXXVIII.—नेता. Some copies of the commentary give",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "पुरोहित मन्त्री प्रधानः as renderings for this. Râmarshi has शिक्षकः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "पालयिता इत्यर्थः. Teacher or director seems to be the preferable",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "rendering. प्रहरण = weapon. Compare the analogous forms चरण, श्रवण",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "&c. ऐश्वर्यबल may be taken as either a Tatpurusha or a Dvandva",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "compound. धिग्धिग्वृथापौरुषम् Râmarshi says पौरुषं बलं धिग्धिक् अस्तु",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "यतः वृथा निरर्थकम्. This is not sufficiently close to the text.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "There are, I think, two ways of taking the words before us; धिक्धिक्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "as an interjection and वृथा पौरुषम् as a separate assertion; or the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "whole thing as meaning “oh fie on abortive valour !”—S'âr-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "dûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXXXIX.—कर्म = acts done in a past life comp. infra Stanzas",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "96, 99, and Vidvanmodatarangiṇî pp. 27, 28. कर्मानुरूपाणि शुभाशुभानि ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "प्राप्नोति सर्वोपि जनः फलानि ॥ आद्यन्तशून्येत्र जगत्प्रवाहे । क्रिया भवेत्कर्मत एव सर्वा ॥",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "कर्मापि पुंसां भवति क्रियातो । बीजाङ्कुरन्यायतया न दोषः ॥ सुविचार्य. The use",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of सु with such a purely verbal form is not common but may",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "be observed now and then. Comp. Nâgânanda (Bomb. Ed.) p.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "18 Sâhityadarpaṇa (Calc. Ed. 1869) p. 124.—Anushṭub.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XC.—The fact of the tree being the ताल (Palm) adds to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "force of the lines as it gives little or no shade.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XCI.—In the Kâvyasangraha this Stanza is given as Vetâla-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "bhaṭṭa’s p. 39.—Drutavilambita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r9",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XCII.—तावत् = प्रथमम्. (commentary) I think सृजति तावत्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "means “does, indeed create but” &c. पुरुषरत्नम् may mean the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "jewel man, or a jewel of a man (i. e. a jewel-like man.) The for-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "mer is preferable.—Drutavilambita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r10",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XCIII.—यदा for यदि is not uncommon. See for one instance",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
